15 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (World maps showing pear and apple distribution and production. Map A indicates pear production, with regions marked by color intensity; red dots represent distribution records. Map B displays apple production similarly, with a higher maximum tonnage. Both maps highlight production areas across North America, Europe, and Asia, with scale bars and a compass for orientation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (World maps showing habitat suitability predictions for different time periods and scenarios. The top map shows current suitability with highly suitable areas in red, moderately suitable in orange, lowly suitable in green, and unsuitable in white. The subsequent maps predict changes for 2030s and 2050s under scenarios SSP1-2.6, SSP2-4.5, and SSP5-8.5, with similar color coding.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (World maps depicting crop suitability and presence under different climate scenarios. Top map shows current conditions. Subsequent maps analyze scenarios for the 2030s and 2050s under SSP1-2.6, SSP2-4.5, and SSP5-8.5. Legends indicate crop absence or presence and suitability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Map and data visualizations of Xinjiang and Gansu regions. Panel A displays yearly data \(2015-2022\) with color coding. Panel B shows host production areas in blue. Panel C illustrates MESS values with routes and bootstrap values. Panel D presents a histogram of total route lengths, with frequency distribution between 90 and 130 units.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Map of China showing vegetation change over time. Shades from green to red indicate areas with increased vegetation loss, with green representing zero years and red representing twenty years. Most notable changes occur in central regions, with northern areas less affected. Legend and scale are provided.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Two comparative line charts \(A and B\) display various economic losses and savings in million dollars. Each chart has categories: losses due to decline in production, decline in quality, economic loss without control, control costs, losses after control measures, losses under control scenarios, and losses saving after control. Data points are marked for 2.5% value, mean value, and 97.5% value, showing financial implications of control measures.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
